{"shortDescription":"By Sudeshna Ghoshal and Ragini MathurMost Latin American stocks rose on Wednesday as a rally in commodity prices and a broader return to risk-taking helped investors look past a stronger dollar and lingering concerns over US interest rates.Investors were also awaiting MSCI's November index review l…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Sudeshna Ghoshal and Ragini Mathur"]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American stocks rose on Wednesday as a rally in commodity prices and a broader return to risk-taking helped investors look past a stronger dollar and lingering concerns over US interest rates."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors were also awaiting MSCI's November index review later in the day, after the index provider warned last month it could downgrade Indonesia from emerging-market to \"standalone\" status."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Brazil, the government is expected to unveil measures in the coming days aimed at delivering a fiscal adjustment equivalent to 0.5% of gross domestic product in 2027, a government source said on Tuesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["The move follows a selloff in Brazilian markets last month after President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva's reelection, as investors questioned whether the government could deliver sufficient fiscal tightening to stabilize public debt."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazil's central bank said on Tuesday that slowing growth could help contain the inflationary effects of recent supply shocks, reinforcing expectations that policymakers may keep interest rates unchanged despite a worsening price outlook."]},{"type":"p","children":["The real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," rose 0.4%, while the Bovespa ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," gained 0.8%."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Looking at the start of the past four easing cycles suggests policymakers will only cut the Selic rate once inflation expectations have fallen materially,\" said William Jackson, chief emerging markets economist at Capital Economics."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"The tried-and-tested way of achieving that in Brazil's recent history is through credible fiscal reforms that improve public finances.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's Latin America equity index (.MILA00000PUS) climbed about 1%, while the regional currency index (.MILA00000CUS) edged up 0.5% after hitting a seven-month low on Tuesday."]},{"type":"p","children":["The previous session's losses followed a hotter-than-expected US inflation report, which bolstered expectations that the Federal Reserve could maintain a hawkish stance and put the focus on speculation of a larger 50-basis-point rate hike in December."]},{"type":"p","children":["The dollar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}}," extended its advance, reaching a four-week high."]},{"type":"p","children":["While a stronger dollar typically pressures emerging-market assets, Latin American markets drew support from rising oil and metals prices, as well as a broader risk-on tone fueled by renewed optimism over artificial intelligence-related trades."]},{"type":"p","children":["Mexican stocks ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMV:ME","text":"BMV:ME"}}," hit a record high, rising 0.9%, while the peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDMXN","text":"FX_IDC:USDMXN"}}," fell 0.1%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Data showed industrial activity declined more than expected in September, marking its weakest performance since October 2024 as construction and manufacturing weakened."]},{"type":"p","children":["Colombian stocks bucked the regional trend, with the equity benchmark falling 0.9% and the peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCOP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCOP"}}," slipping 0.3%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Colombia's economy likely slowed in the third quarter, hurt by the dea